#* {{RQ:Besant Ivory Gate|chapter=Prologue|page=16|passage=Athelstan Arundel walked home all the way, foaming and raging. {{...}} He walked the '''whole''' way, walking through crowds, and under the noses of dray-horses, carriage-horses, and cart-horses, without taking the least notice of them.}}
